IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the employee receiving a benefit meets:
-- whether it is a "fringe benefit" (s 136(1)); the exemptions an employee most often meets -- an electric car (s 8A), work
-- related items such as a phone or laptop (s 58X), minor benefits under $300 (s 58P), loans for work expenses and on
-- arm's length terms (s 17(1), (3)); the taxable value of a car under the statutory formula (s 9) and of a loan (s 18);
-- and the reportable fringe benefits amount that appears on the employee's income statement (ss 135N, 135P), with the
-- rate of tax it uses (Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986 ss 6, 6A).
--
-- SEAT: the employee receiving the benefit. "My employer gives me a car, a loan, a phone or a gift: is it a fringe benefit,
-- is it exempt, what is its taxable value, and what will show on my income statement?" The tax itself falls on the
-- employer (s 66); the employer's questions are in the seat layer fbtaa-seat-employer.l4, which imports this module.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 97, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 49, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00332), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03280.txt. The formulas in ss 5B(1B), 5B(1C), 9(1) and
-- 135P(2) were images the text deposit dropped; they are transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03280.formulas.md
-- from the authorised Word rendering of the same compilation, and encoded from there.
--
-- THE RATE OF TAX is set by the Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986, Compilation No. 9 (19 June 2018), deposited at
-- ../../../fringe-benefits-tax-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03281.txt: 47% (s 6), plus 2 percentage points for the
-- years of tax starting 1 April 2015 and 1 April 2016 (s 6A). Brought in as those figures. A year of tax before 1 April 2015
-- answers `not covered` (the earlier rates are not in that compilation).
--
-- NUMBERS NOT IN THE ACT are inputs: the benchmark interest rate (the Reserve Bank's published rate, "statutory interest
-- rate", s 136(1)), the GST rate (the GST Act's), and any judgment the Act leaves to someone else (whether it would be
-- "unreasonable" to treat a minor benefit as a fringe benefit, s 58P(1)(f)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The other benefit types (debt waiver, expense payment, housing, living-away-from-home, board, meal
-- entertainment, car parking, property, residual) and their valuation; the cost basis for cars (s 10); the otherwise
-- deductible rules (ss 19, 24, 37, 44, 52); the other exemptions (ss 8, 17(2), (4), 21-22, 41, 47, 53-58ZE except 58P and
-- 58X); remote area reductions (ss 59-65CC); the rebate (s 65J); ss 57A and 58 employers (the employee's reportable amount
-- under s 135Q answers `not covered`); assessments, collection and administration except the return and payment dates.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the employee's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 -- the employee receiving a benefit`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986 ss 6, 6A as compiled in 2018
    `the deposited Fringe Benefits Tax Act gives the rate only for years of tax from 1 April 2015`
    -- s 135Q
    `the reportable amount for an employee of a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or a s 58 employer is worked out under s 135Q, which is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `The rate of tax -- Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986 ss 6, 6A`

-- s 6: "The rate of tax ... is 47%." s 6A(2): "Increase the rate of tax mentioned in section 6 by 2 percentage points" for
-- "(a) the year of tax starting on 1 April 2015; (b) the year of tax starting on 1 April 2016". A year of tax is named by the
-- calendar year in which it starts (s 136(1): "the year starting on 1 April").
GIVEN `the year of tax starting in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the rate of fringe benefits tax for` MEANS
    IF `the year of tax starting in` LESS THAN 2015
    THEN `not covered` `the deposited Fringe Benefits Tax Act gives the rate only for years of tax from 1 April 2015`
    ELSE IF `the year of tax starting in` EQUALS 2015 OR `the year of tax starting in` EQUALS 2016
         THEN `answered` 0.49
         ELSE `answered` 0.47

§§ `s 136(1) -- is it a fringe benefit`

-- s 136(1) "fringe benefit ... means a benefit ... provided to the employee or to an associate of the employee by: (c) the
-- employer; or (d) an associate of the employer; or (e)" a third party under an arrangement with the employer or its
-- associate, "or (ea)" a third party where the employer or associate knowingly participates in or facilitates it, "in respect
-- of the employment of the employee, but does not include: (f) a payment of salary or wages ...; (g) a benefit that is an
-- exempt benefit ...; (h) ... an ESS interest under an employee share scheme ...; (j)" a contribution to a complying
-- superannuation fund for the employee; "(k) a superannuation benefit"; "(lb) a genuine redundancy payment; or (lc) an
-- employment termination payment"; and the other exclusions in (l)-(s). "associate": s 318 of the ITAA 1936 (a borrowed term).
DECLARE `What the benefit is` IS ONE OF
    `salary or wages`
    `a contribution to a complying superannuation fund for me`
    `shares or rights under an employee share scheme`
    `a genuine redundancy payment or employment termination payment`
    `something else (a car, a loan, goods, a payment of my expenses, a gift, housing, and so on)`

DECLARE `Is it a fringe benefit` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is a fringe benefit, provided in respect of my employment; my employer is liable for fringe benefits tax on its taxable value (ss 66, 136(1))`
    `no: it is an exempt benefit, so it is not a fringe benefit (s 136(1)(g))`
    `no: salary or wages, super contributions, employee share scheme interests and termination payments are excluded from "fringe benefit" (s 136(1)(f)-(lc)); they are taxed, if at all, under the income tax law`
    `no: it is not provided to me or my associate by my employer, its associate, or a third party under an arrangement with or facilitated by them (s 136(1)(c)-(ea))`
    `no: it is not provided in respect of my employment (s 136(1))`

@export Is this benefit I have received a "fringe benefit"?
GIVEN `it is provided to me or my associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the benefit is provided to you, or to an associate of yours (for example your spouse or child)
      `my employer is behind it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided by your employer (or a former or future employer), by an associate of your employer, or by someone else under an arrangement with your employer or its associate, or with your employer knowingly taking part in or facilitating it
      `it is because of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided in respect of your employment (because you are, were or will be the employee), rather than for some unrelated reason
      `what the benefit is` IS A `What the benefit is` @desc What the benefit is
      `it is an exempt benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an exempt benefit under the Act (for example an electric car under s 8A, a work phone or laptop under s 58X, a minor benefit under s 58P; see those questions)
GIVETH A `Is it a fringe benefit`
`Is this benefit a fringe benefit` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it is provided to me or my associate` AND `my employer is behind it`))
    THEN `no: it is not provided to me or my associate by my employer, its associate, or a third party under an arrangement with or facilitated by them (s 136(1)(c)-(ea))`
    ELSE IF (NOT `it is because of my employment`)
         THEN `no: it is not provided in respect of my employment (s 136(1))`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`what the benefit is` EQUALS `something else (a car, a loan, goods, a payment of my expenses, a gift, housing, and so on)`))
              THEN `no: salary or wages, super contributions, employee share scheme interests and termination payments are excluded from "fringe benefit" (s 136(1)(f)-(lc)); they are taxed, if at all, under the income tax law`
              ELSE IF `it is an exempt benefit`
                   THEN `no: it is an exempt benefit, so it is not a fringe benefit (s 136(1)(g))`
                   ELSE `yes: it is a fringe benefit, provided in respect of my employment; my employer is liable for fringe benefits tax on its taxable value (ss 66, 136(1))`

§§ `Exemptions -- ss 8A, 58X, 58P, 17`

-- s 8A(1): a car benefit is exempt if "(a) the benefit is provided in the year of tax in respect of the employment of a
-- current employee; and (b) the car is a zero or low emissions vehicle when the benefit is provided; and (c) no amount of
-- luxury car tax ... has become payable on a supply ... or importation ... of the car before the benefit is provided".
-- (2)-(4): a battery electric vehicle ("uses only an electric motor for propulsion" with neither a fuel cell nor an internal
-- combustion engine) or a hydrogen fuel cell electric vehicle (no internal combustion engine). A plug-in hybrid has an
-- internal combustion engine, so it is neither. s 135P(3): the exempt car still counts for the reportable amount.
DECLARE `The kind of car` IS ONE OF
    `a battery electric vehicle (electric motor only, no fuel cell or petrol or diesel engine)`
    `a hydrogen fuel cell electric vehicle (no petrol or diesel engine)`
    `a plug-in hybrid`
    `a petrol, diesel or other car`

DECLARE `Is my car exempt` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the car benefit is exempt (s 8A), but its taxable value still counts towards my reportable fringe benefits amount (s 135P(3))`
    `no: only a battery electric or hydrogen fuel cell electric vehicle is a zero or low emissions vehicle (s 8A(2)-(4)); a plug-in hybrid or other car is not`
    `no: luxury car tax became payable on the car before the benefit was provided (s 8A(1)(c))`
    `no: the exemption is only for a current employee (s 8A(1)(a))`

@export Is the car my employer provides me exempt from fringe benefits tax as an electric car?
GIVEN `I am a current employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a current employee of the employer (you receive, or are entitled to receive, salary or wages)
      `the kind of car` IS A `The kind of car` @desc What kind of car it is, when the benefit is provided
      `luxury car tax was payable on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether luxury car tax became payable on a supply or importation of the car before the benefit was provided
GIVETH A `Is my car exempt`
`Is my electric car exempt` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am a current employee`)
    THEN `no: the exemption is only for a current employee (s 8A(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF `the kind of car` EQUALS `a plug-in hybrid` OR `the kind of car` EQUALS `a petrol, diesel or other car`
         THEN `no: only a battery electric or hydrogen fuel cell electric vehicle is a zero or low emissions vehicle (s 8A(2)-(4)); a plug-in hybrid or other car is not`
         ELSE IF `luxury car tax was payable on it`
              THEN `no: luxury car tax became payable on the car before the benefit was provided (s 8A(1)(c))`
              ELSE `yes: the car benefit is exempt (s 8A), but its taxable value still counts towards my reportable fringe benefits amount (s 135P(3))`

-- s 58X(1): an expense payment, property or residual benefit "provided by an employer to an employee ... in respect of the
-- employee's employment is an exempt benefit" where the item is an eligible work related item. (2): "Each of the following
-- is an eligible work related item if it is primarily for use in the employee's employment and it is not provided to the
-- employee under a salary packaging arrangement: (a) a portable electronic device; (b) an item of computer software; (c) an
-- item of protective clothing; (d) a briefcase; (e) a tool of trade."
DECLARE `The work item` IS ONE OF
    `a portable electronic device (a phone, laptop or tablet)`
    `computer software`
    `protective clothing`
    `a briefcase`
    `a tool of trade`
    `something else`

@export Is the phone, laptop, software, protective clothing, briefcase or tool my employer gives me (or pays for) exempt?
GIVEN `the work item` IS A `The work item` @desc What the item is
      `it is mainly for my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is primarily for use in your employment
      `it is part of a salary packaging arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided to you under a salary packaging (salary sacrifice) arrangement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work item exempt` IF
        (NOT (`the work item` EQUALS `something else`))
    AND `it is mainly for my work`
    AND (NOT `it is part of a salary packaging arrangement`)

-- s 58P(1): a benefit is exempt where "(e) the notional taxable value of the minor benefit ... is less than $300; and (f)
-- having regard to" how infrequent and irregular such benefits are, their total value, the practical difficulty of valuing
-- them, and the circumstances (an unexpected event; not mainly a reward for services), "it would be concluded that it would be
-- unreasonable to treat the minor benefit as a fringe benefit"; and (c) an expense payment, property or residual benefit
-- must not be one that would be an in-house fringe benefit. Paragraph (f) is a judgment; asked as a fact.
@export Is this small gift or benefit from my employer exempt as a minor benefit (under $300)?
GIVEN `its value` IS A NUMBER @desc The notional taxable value of the benefit (roughly what it would be taxed on), in dollars
      `it would be unreasonable to treat it as a fringe benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, given how rarely and irregularly such benefits are given, their total value, how hard they are to value, and the circumstances (for example help with an unexpected event, rather than a reward for work), it would be unreasonable to treat it as a fringe benefit
      `it is goods or services from my employer's own business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an expense payment, property or residual benefit that would be an in-house fringe benefit (goods or services of a kind your employer's business provides to the public)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my minor benefit exempt` IF
        `its value` LESS THAN 300
    AND `it would be unreasonable to treat it as a fringe benefit`
    AND (NOT `it is goods or services from my employer's own business`)

-- s 17(1): a loan by a person whose business includes lending to the public is exempt if its interest rate is fixed in a
-- document when made, not less than on a similar arm's length loan to the public, and cannot be varied. s 17(3): an advance
-- by an employer to a current employee whose "sole purpose" is to meet expenses of the employment incurred within 6 months,
-- not substantially exceeding them, which the employee must account for within 6 months and repay any balance of.
DECLARE `What kind of loan` IS ONE OF
    `an advance to pay expenses of my job`
    `a fixed-rate loan from a lender to the public, on its ordinary terms`
    `another loan`

@export Is a loan from my employer exempt from fringe benefits tax?
GIVEN `what kind of loan` IS A `What kind of loan` @desc What the loan is
      `the conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a job-expenses advance: you are a current employee, it is solely to meet work expenses incurred within 6 months, it does not substantially exceed them, and you must account for them and repay the rest within 6 months. For a lender's loan: its rate was set in writing when made, is not below the rate on a similar arm's length loan to the public, and cannot be varied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan exempt` IF
        (NOT (`what kind of loan` EQUALS `another loan`))
    AND `the conditions are met`

§§ `Taxable value -- s 9 (car, statutory formula), s 18 (loan)`

-- s 9(1) (formula from the sidecar): (Base value of the car x 0.2 x Number of days during that year of tax on which the car
-- fringe benefits were provided by the provider / Number of days in that year of tax) - Amount (if any) of the recipient's
-- payment. s 9(2)(a): base value is the cost price (or leased car value) at the earliest holding time times B, where B is
-- 2/3 "in a case where the commencement of the year of tax is later than the fourth anniversary of the earliest holding
-- time" and 1 otherwise, plus the cost price of non-business accessories fitted later. (e): the recipient's payment is what
-- the employee paid towards the car (net of reimbursement). A year of tax runs 1 April to 31 March. A recipient's payment
-- larger than the formula's first term is read as reducing the taxable value to nil, not below (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `the year of tax starting in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the year of tax` MEANS
    (Day (Date 1 4 (`the year of tax starting in` PLUS 1))) MINUS (Day (Date 1 4 `the year of tax starting in`))

GIVEN `the cost price` IS A NUMBER
      `the day first held` IS A DATE
      `the year of tax starting in` IS A NUMBER
      `the accessories` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base value of the car` MEANS
    IF (Date 1 4 `the year of tax starting in`) GREATER THAN (`add years` `the day first held` 4)
    THEN (`the cost price` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3) PLUS `the accessories`
    ELSE `the cost price` PLUS `the accessories`

GIVEN `the cost price` IS A NUMBER
      `the day first held` IS A DATE
      `the year of tax starting in` IS A NUMBER
      `the accessories` IS A NUMBER
      `the days provided` IS A NUMBER
      `the recipient's payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory formula taxable value` MEANS
    IF `the gross value` GREATER THAN `the recipient's payment`
    THEN `the gross value` MINUS `the recipient's payment`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the gross value` MEANS
            (`the base value of the car` `the cost price` `the day first held` `the year of tax starting in` `the accessories` TIMES 0.2)
            TIMES (`the days provided` DIVIDED BY `the number of days in the year of tax` `the year of tax starting in`)

@export What is the taxable value of the car my employer provides me, under the statutory formula?
GIVEN `the car's cost price` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost price of the car to your employer (or its associate) when they first held it, or its leased car value then if leased (GST-inclusive, without registration or stamp duty)
      `the day my employer first held the car` IS A DATE @desc The earliest day your employer (or its associate) held the car
      `the year of tax starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts (the FBT year runs from 1 April to 31 March; 2026 means 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)
      `the cost of non-business accessories added` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost price of non-business accessories (for example a tow bar for private use) fitted after your employer first held the car and still fitted during the year; 0 if none
      `the days the car was available to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which the car was provided to you (available for your private use)
      `what I paid towards the car` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid towards the car during the year and were not reimbursed (for example fuel you paid for, if you gave your employer the declaration or receipts in time)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The taxable value of my car` MEANS
    `the statutory formula taxable value` `the car's cost price` `the day my employer first held the car` `the year of tax starting in` `the cost of non-business accessories added` `the days the car was available to me` `what I paid towards the car`

-- s 18(1): "the amount (if any) by which the notional amount of interest in relation to the loan in respect of the year of tax
-- exceeds the amount of interest that has accrued on the loan". s 136(1): the notional amount of interest is the interest
-- "calculated on the daily balance of the loan at" the statutory interest rate, which for a year of tax is the benchmark
-- interest rate: "the rate of interest, known as the large bank housing lenders variable interest rate on loans for housing
-- for owner occupation, last published by the Reserve Bank of Australia before the commencement of the year of tax" (an
-- input). The daily balance is taken as constant, and a day's interest as 1/365 of a year's (NOTES.md finding 5).
@export What is the taxable value of a cheap or interest-free loan from my employer?
GIVEN `the loan balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you owed on the loan each day (taken as the same through the period)
      `the days I owed it in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which you were obliged to repay the loan
      `the benchmark interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory interest rate for the FBT year, as a percentage: the Reserve Bank's large bank housing lenders variable rate for owner-occupied housing last published before 1 April
      `the interest that accrued on the loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest that actually accrued on the loan for the year (0 for an interest-free loan)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The taxable value of my loan` MEANS
    IF `the notional interest` GREATER THAN `the interest that accrued on the loan`
    THEN `the notional interest` MINUS `the interest that accrued on the loan`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the notional interest` MEANS `the loan balance` TIMES (`the benchmark interest rate` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES (`the days I owed it in the year` DIVIDED BY 365)

§§ `The reportable fringe benefits amount -- ss 135N, 135P (what shows on my income statement)`

-- s 135P(1): an employee has a reportable fringe benefits amount for a year of income if the individual fringe benefits
-- amount for the year of tax ending on 31 March in that year of income "is more than $2,000". (2) (formula from the
-- sidecar): Individual fringe benefits amount x 1 / (1 - Rate of tax for the year of tax). (3): an exempt electric car's
-- taxable value is counted. s 5E(2)-(3): the individual fringe benefits amount is the employee's share of the taxable values
-- of fringe benefits, leaving out excluded fringe benefits (car parking, meal entertainment not salary packaged, and others).
-- s 135N: the reportable fringe benefits total is the sum over all employers. s 135Q (employers under ss 57A, 58) is not
-- encoded.
@export What is my reportable fringe benefits amount for this employer (shown on my income statement)?
GIVEN `my individual fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of the fringe benefits provided to you by this employer in the FBT year (1 April to 31 March), including an exempt electric car, but leaving out car parking, meal entertainment that is not salary packaged, and the other excluded fringe benefits
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which that FBT year started (the year of income is the one ending 30 June after the FBT year ends)
      `my employer is a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or an employer of the kind in s 58 (government, religious or non-profit care of the elderly or disadvantaged)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`My reportable fringe benefits amount` MEANS
    IF `my employer is a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer`
    THEN `not covered` `the reportable amount for an employee of a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or a s 58 employer is worked out under s 135Q, which is not encoded`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the rate of fringe benefits tax for` `the FBT year starting in`
         WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
         WHEN `answered` rate THEN
             IF `my individual fringe benefits amount` GREATER THAN 2000
             THEN `answered` (`my individual fringe benefits amount` TIMES (1 DIVIDED BY (1 MINUS rate)))
             ELSE `answered` 0

@export What is my reportable fringe benefits total for the year (all my employers together)?
GIVEN `my reportable amounts from each employer` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc Your reportable fringe benefits amount from each employer for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
`My reportable fringe benefits total` MEANS sum `my reportable amounts from each employer`
